Nxe4 Bxe4 28. Rxe4 Qd5 29. Re1 Rxc4 30. Qb2 c1=Q {Sources: The Field, 22 Aug
1914; 'The Chess Amateur', Sept 1914; Times Literary Supplement, 17 Sept 1914;
BCM, Oct 1914; 'The Year-Book of Chess 1914' - M W Stevens - F Hollings,
London, and W Hill, Chicago (1915); Brighton and Hove Gazette, 20 Aug 1971.
Also published in the Borough of West Ham, East Ham and Stratford Express, 5
Sept 1914, where the game ends after White's 30th move.} 0-1

